---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Ambiguous = `Bill, tip percent, how many people. Tell me what each
person owes. And round it up.`;

const Questions = `Questions this brief does not answer

  - What order do the three values go in?
  - Round up to the nearest cent, or the nearest pound?
  - The rounded shares will not add up to the bill exactly.
    Do I say so, or quietly absorb it?
  - What if the tip is 0? What if there is one person?

MY DECISIONS
  - Order: bill, tipPercent, people. Written at the top of the file.
  - Round up to the nearest cent.
  - Report the collected total so the discrepancy is visible.`;

const pool = [
  { slug: "cc-name-badge", title: "Name Badge", stars: 1, after: "2.2" },
  { slug: "cc-temperature-band", title: "Temperature Band", stars: 1, after: "2.3" },
  { slug: "cc-unit-price", title: "Unit Price", stars: 1, after: "2.3" },
  { slug: "cc-grade-band", title: "Grade Band", stars: 2, after: "2.3" },
  { slug: "cc-tip-split", title: "Tip Split", stars: 2, after: "2.5" },
  { slug: "cc-fuel-check", title: "Fuel Check", stars: 2, after: "2.5" },
  { slug: "cc-progress-bar", title: "Progress Bar", stars: 2, after: "2.5" },
  { slug: "cc-dice-roller", title: "Dice Roller", stars: 2, after: "2.5" },
  { slug: "cc-receipt-total", title: "Receipt Total", stars: 3, after: "2.6" },
  { slug: "cc-word-wrap", title: "Line Splitter", stars: 3, after: "2.6" },
];

const bonus = [
  { slug: "cc-roman-numerals", title: "Roman Numerals", stars: 3, after: "2.6" },
  { slug: "cc-histogram", title: "Histogram", stars: 3, after: "2.6" },
];
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge Set 5</h1>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">Complete any 5 of the 10 below.</h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>What This Set Is For</h2>

          <p>
            <b>Every challenge here is a procedure with a parameter that changes
            what it does.</b> That is not a coincidence and it is not a theme
            chosen for variety.
          </p>

          <p>
            It is the exact wording of a Create Performance Task requirement:
            <i>a student-developed procedure with one or more parameters that
            have an effect on the functionality of the procedure.</i> You will
            write that procedure for real in Quarter 3. This set is where you
            write it thirty times first, while it costs nothing.
          </p>

          <p>
            Same rule as always: <b>write your requirements list before you
            write any code</b>, and submit both.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="shape">
          <h2>This Set Is About Deciding the Shape</h2>

          <p>
            In Quarter 1 the thing a brief left open was a value, or a boundary.
            Here it is almost always <b>the shape of the procedure itself</b>
            &mdash; how many parameters, in what order, and whether it returns
            or prints.
          </p>

          <Code
            code={Ambiguous}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="From the Tip Split brief"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-4">
            Read that and notice it never says what the procedure looks like.
            Here is what should end up in your requirements list:
          </p>

          <Code
            code={Questions}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="Requirements — the questions half"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-4">
            <b>Parameter order is the one that will bite you.</b> JavaScript
            matches arguments by position and says nothing when you get it
            wrong &mdash; you get a plausible number computed from the wrong
            values. Write the order down before you write the procedure, and
            put it in a comment above the definition.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>Return or print is the other one.</b> A procedure that prints
            cannot be used inside another expression. If a brief hints that its
            answer will be used for something else, it needs to return.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="challenges">
          <h2>The Challenges</h2>

          <p>Pick <b>any five</b>.</p>

          <ul class="list-unstyled mt-4">
            {
              pool.map((c) => (
                <li class="mb-2">
                  <i class="si-terminal text-sn-theme me-2"></i>
                  <a href={`/courses/ap-csp/unit-2/${c.slug}`}>{c.title}</a>
                  <span class="ms-2">
                    {Array.from({ length: c.stars }).map(() => (
                      <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
                    ))}
                  </span>
                  <span class="text-body-secondary ms-2">
                    &mdash; after Activity {c.after}
                  </span>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="bonus">
          <h2>If Five Is Not Enough</h2>

          <p>
            These two are <b>extra credit</b>, worth 3 points each on top of the
            set.
          </p>

          <ul class="list-unstyled mt-4">
            {
              bonus.map((c) => (
                <li class="mb-2">
                  <i class="si-flask text-sn-yellow me-2"></i>
                  <a href={`/courses/ap-csp/unit-2/${c.slug}`}>{c.title}</a>
                  <span class="ms-2">
                    {Array.from({ length: c.stars }).map(() => (
                      <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
                    ))}
                  </span>
                  <span class="text-body-secondary ms-2">
                    &mdash; after Activity {c.after}
                  </span>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>

          <p class="mt-3">
            <b>Roman Numerals punishes coding before thinking.</b> Work the
            algorithm out on paper first; the subtractive cases are where every
            attempt breaks.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="start-here">
          <h2>If the Part 4 Quiz Went Badly</h2>

          <p>
            These three are the repair kit. <b>They count toward your five</b>
            &mdash; this is not extra work, it is a different order to do it in.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>
              <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-2/cc-temperature-band">Temperature Band</a>
              &mdash; returning instead of printing
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-2/cc-name-badge">Name Badge</a>
              &mdash; what a parameter is for
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-2/cc-receipt-total">Receipt Total</a>
              &mdash; composition, once the first two make sense
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>For <b>each</b> challenge you complete, submit:</p>

          <ol>
            <li>
              <b>Your requirements list</b> &mdash; including the parameter
              order you chose and whether the procedure returns or prints.
            </li>
            <li><b>Your program file.</b></li>
          </ol>

          <p>
            This set is worth <b>5 points</b>, graded on completion. Extra
            credit is on top and does not replace any of the five.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Commence Challenges
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
